WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.200
MARKUS KLUTE: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.890
So in the last two videos, we
looked at the Dirac equation

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.750
and we looked at
solutions Dirac equations.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.350
And in the last
lecture we found that,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.240
along with positive
energy states,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.870
we had those negative
energy states.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.060
Since we cannot simply drop
them or disregard them,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.880
we do have to find physical
interpretation for these

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.870
negative energy solutions.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.250
The first one which
was put forward,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.460
is the one where you think
about negative energy

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.680
states all being populated--

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.570
and that is the vacuum.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.560
The vacuum is basically a sea
full of negative energy states

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.540
which are all populated.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.720
So if you have a
positive energy state,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.330
and there are electrons sitting
in this energy state here,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.030
the electron, because of the
Pauli exclusion principle

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.870
cannot fall down into the
negative energy state.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.420
But you are able to kick
them out, for example,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.190
to excite them with a photon.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.390
Very excited.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.210
The negative energy state,
you get an electron out.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.690
This process is then
will lend to the creation

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:13.544
of a positron and an
electron pair with a photon.

00:01:13.544 --> 00:01:15.620
[INAUDIBLE] pair production.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.310
It can also explain
undulation where

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.740
there's an empty and
a negative energy

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:26.060
stage where the electron just
folds into creating a photon.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.490
So while the
interpretation is useful

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:32.450
and it explains pair production
and undulation processes,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.230
they fail to explain
what this vacuum,

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:40.050
the sea of negative
energy state even is.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.310
So a more useful interpretation
is one part forward that

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.400
Feynman and Stückelberg, which
came out of the discussion

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.260
of quantum field theory.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.215
And we already discussed
this interpretation

00:01:50.215 --> 00:01:52.980
when we looked at
Feynman [INAUDIBLE]..

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.920
So have a look at
this Feynman diagram

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.370
here where you have an
electron with a positive energy

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.740
and an electron with
a negative energy,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.080
building a photon,
which is twice

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:08.509
the energy in the symmetric
configuration of the electrons

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:10.400
before.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.590
And you're interpreting the
negative energy solution

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:18.650
here of the electron as the
electron moving backward

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.580
in time.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.260
This is an equivalent to a
positron with a positive energy

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.630
and an electron with
a positive energy

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:30.800
where the positron and the
electron move forward in time.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.710
Again, in both cases, you
see the energy of the photon

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:38.760
is two times the energy
of those two particles.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:39.340
All right.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.490
So this is a very
short discussion.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:45.330
And we will see later on
how we use the spinodes

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.570
for antiparticles together with
spinodes for particles order

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.165
to make relations that
could have matrix element.

00:02:51.165 --> 00:02:56.100
And so we move forward with our
discussion of Feynman rules,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.170
this time now, with
spin-1/2 particles included.

